            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93748",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "http-cache-semantics: http-cache-semantics: Information Disclosure via max-stale directive"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "http-cache-semantics through 4.2.0 fails to properly validate security-zeroed cache entries when processing client max-stale directives, allowing unauthenticated attackers to retrieve cached responses belonging to other users. Attackers can request the same URL with a large max-stale value to obtain another user's Set-Cookie session credentials from shared-cache entries that were deliberately zeroed for security reasons."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93748",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93748\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: http-cache-semantics\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93748](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93748)\nhttp-cache-semantics through 4.2.0 fails to properly validate security-zeroed cache entries when processing client max-stale directives, allowing unauthenticated attackers to retrieve cached responses belonging to other users. Attackers can request the same URL with a large max-stale value to obtain another user's Set-Cookie session credentials from shared-cache entries that were deliberately zeroed for security reasons.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93748**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|http-cache-semantics||[CVE-2026-93748](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93748)|\n\nhttp-cache-semantics through 4.2.0 fails to properly validate security-zeroed cache entries when processing client max-stale directives, allowing unauthenticated attackers to retrieve cached responses belonging to other users. Attackers can request the same URL with a large max-stale value to obtain another user's Set-Cookie session credentials from shared-cache entries that were deliberately zeroed for security reasons."
