            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59874",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "tar: Node-tar: Denial of Service via malformed tar archive header"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "node-tar is a tar archive manipulation library for Node.js. Prior to 7.5.18, tar.replace accepts a checksum-valid tar header with a negative base-256 encoded entry size, causing the archive scanner to make no progress while repeatedly parsing the same header. This issue is fixed in version 7.5.18."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59874",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59874\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: tar\nFixed Version: 7.5.18\nLink: [CVE-2026-59874](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59874)\nnode-tar is a tar archive manipulation library for Node.js. Prior to 7.5.18, tar.replace accepts a checksum-valid tar header with a negative base-256 encoded entry size, causing the archive scanner to make no progress while repeatedly parsing the same header. This issue is fixed in version 7.5.18.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59874**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|tar|7.5.18|[CVE-2026-59874](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59874)|\n\nnode-tar is a tar archive manipulation library for Node.js. Prior to 7.5.18, tar.replace accepts a checksum-valid tar header with a negative base-256 encoded entry size, causing the archive scanner to make no progress while repeatedly parsing the same header. This issue is fixed in version 7.5.18."
              },
